      "title": {
        "en": "Patient and expert training team"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet parents overwhelmingly praise head trainers Sarah and Katrina for their warm, knowledgeable, and patient guidance. Reviewers highlight their positive reinforcement methods and ability to provide tailored coaching in small class settings. Handlers appreciate that the instructors take time to answer individual questions and build confidence in both dogs and their humans."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "results",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 16,
      "title": {
        "en": "Noticeable progress in canine skills"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Clients report significant improvements in obedience, loose-leash walking, and puppy manners after only a few training sessions. Dog owners particularly appreciate practical real-world exercises and introductory scent work classes that stimulate problem-solving. Reviewers emphasize that foundational puppy courses successfully turn shy or overexcited dogs into focused companions."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 16,
      "title": {
        "en": "Safe and structured socialization"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Reviewers consistently commend the supervised puppy play sessions, noting how carefully the trainers evaluate play styles, temperaments, and energy levels. Pet owners observe that timid puppies quickly overcome anxiety in the calm, controlled indoor studio. Handlers value the force-free environment where dogs learn healthy interaction without feeling overwhelmed."
      }
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "What training methods are used at The Dog School?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "The school uses force-free, positive reinforcement techniques designed to build confidence, focus, and a strong bond between dogs and their handlers."
      },
      "basis": "both"
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "How are puppy play sessions organized?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Puppy socialization sessions are closely supervised in small groups, with trainers carefully matching pups based on size, play style, and energy level."
      },
      "basis": "reviews"
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "Can clients book single drop-in training classes?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Yes, the studio offers flexible credit packages allowing handlers to book individual drop-in classes that suit their weekly schedules."
      },
      "basis": "both"
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "What age group is eligible for puppy socialization?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "The puppy training and socialization programs are specifically designed for young puppies between 8 and 16 weeks of age."
